<title>GERMANY: DG Bank 96 operating profit up 66 pct.</title>
<headline>DG Bank 96 operating profit up 66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    868.7  vs 523.9</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions		     165.2  vs 312.2</p>
<p>    Group own-account trading profit	187.2  vs 182.6</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 3,300  vs 2,771</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     240.5  vs 287.8</p>
<p>    Group administration costs		2,672  vs 2,467</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total	     331,300 vs 291,200</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German cooperative bank is Deutsche Genossenschaftsbank. The bank said it planned to pay an unchanged dividend. For 1995 the bank paid a dividend of 2.75 percent on a net basis and eight percent on a gross basis. The results are provisional.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
